#
# Conformance case: teleology/invariant-breach-denies-action.
#
# An action schema declares a logic:invariant (balanced) the action must preserve.
# At the probed state the precondition (ready) holds but the invariant does NOT obtain:
# the gate verdict is logic:GateDenied with a denial reason naming the breached
# invariant and the schema's compensation (rollback). A breached invariant is a hard,
# surfaced denial — never a silent pass.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/invariant-breach-denies-action/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
